column1:
2:23|“How can you say, ‘I am not defiled;
I have not followed the Baals’?
Look at your path in the valley;
know what you have done,
you swift young she-camel zigzagging on her paths,|Retains female camel image and plural Baals.

4:7|A lion has come out of his thicket;
a destroyer of nations has set out.
He has left his place to devastate your land;
your cities will become ruins without inhabitants.|Keeps invader unnamed and lion comparison.

6:11|I am filled with the **LORD**’s fury;
I am weary of holding it in.
“Pour it out on children in the street
and on gatherings of young men,
for husband and wife alike will be captured,
the old and those full of years.|Marks command after prophet’s complaint and retains vulnerable victims.

6:23|They grip bow and javelin;
they are cruel and show no compassion.
Their voice roars like the sea;
they ride horses, arrayed for battle
against you, Daughter Zion.”|Preserves weapons, cruelty and sea-roar simile.

6:29|The bellows blow fiercely;
the lead is consumed by fire.
The refiner refines for nothing;
the wicked are not separated out.|Follows read fire-consumed division and preserves failed refining.
